ctylifera - Leaning Pine Arboretum - DSC05559.JPG", "description": "Botanical specimen in Leaning Pine Arboretum, California Polytechnic State University, San Luis Obispo, California, USA.", "download_url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Phoenix_dactylifera_-_Leaning_Pine_Arboretum_-_DSC05559.JPG/1920px-Phoenix_dactylifera_-_Leaning_Pine_Arboretum_-_DSC05559.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "original_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/Phoenix_dactylifera_-_Leaning_Pine_Arboretum_-_DSC05559.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "source_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phoenix_dactylifera_-_Leaning_Pine_Arboretum_-_DSC05559.JPG", "credit": "Daderot", "credit_line": "Own work", "license": "CC0", "license_url": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en", "attribution_required": "false", "restrictions": "", "date_created": "2013-11-16 16:58:56", "width": 1600, "height": 1067, "licensing_verified": false, "sha256": "f289e9f663f181634de37a30b282eaf1fe1115677659b0c5d57d4a0abced3586"}}, {"kind": "story", "title": "\u062d\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0645\u0631 \u0646\u0641\u0633\u0647\u0627 \u0641\u064a\u0647\u0627 \u062a\u0641\u0627\u0635\u064a\u0644 \u063a\u0631\u064a\u0628\u0629", "body": "\u0637\u0648\u0644 \u062d\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0645\u0631 \u064a\u062a\u0631\u0627\u0648\u062d \u0628\u064a\u0646 3 \u06487 \u0633\u0645 \u0648\u0642\u0637\u0631\u0647\u0627 \u062d\u0648\u0627\u0644\u064a 2.5 \u0633\u0645\u060c \u0648\u0623\u0644\u0648\u0627\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062a\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641 \u0645\u0646 \u0628\u0646\u064a \u063a\u0627\u0645\u0642 \u0644\u0623\u062d\u0645\u0631 \u0623\u0648 \u0623\u0635\u0641\u0631 \u062d\u0633\u0628 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0648\u0639.", "punch": "", "claim_ids": ["c3"], "image_query": "dates fruit", "image": {"provider": "commons", "asset_id": "15936499", "title": "File:Ripe and dry dates fruit bunches.jpg", "description": "Ripe and dry dates fruit bunches at the Abdul Aziz Date Farm in Medina.", "download_url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Ripe_and_dry_dates_fruit_bunches.jpg/1920px-Ripe_and_dry_dates_fruit_bunches.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "original_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/Ripe_and_dry_dates_fruit_bunches.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "source_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ripe_and_dry_dates_fruit_bunches.jpg", "credit": "Kerina yin", "credit_line": "Own work", "license": "CC0", "license_url": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en", "attribution_required": "false", "restrictions": "", "date_created": "2011-07-05", "width": 1600, "height": 1197, "licensing_verified": false, "sha256": "3653a950364841b3c1b2772b87cc51a23d3ec3bbe0533099cd0103d9bd5762c5"}}, {"kind": "story", "title": "\u0644\u064a\u0634 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0645\u0631 \u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0637\u0627\u0642\u0629 \u0642\u0648\u064a", "body": "\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0645\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062c\u0641\u0641 \u0646\u0633\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0633\u0643\u0631 \u0641\u064a\u0647 \u062a\u0648\u0635\u0644 63 \u0625\u0644\u0649 64% \u0645\u0646 \u0648\u0632\u0646\u0647\u060c \u0648\u0647\u0627\u0644\u0634\u064a \u064a\u0641\u0633\u0631 \u0644\u064a\u0634 \u0646\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645\u0647 \u0643\u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0637\u0627\u0642\u0629 \u0633\u0631\u064a\u0639 \u062e\u0635\u0648\u0635\u0627\u064b \u0648\u0642\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0641\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0641\u064a \u0631\u0645\u0636\u0627\u0646.", "punch": "", "claim_ids": ["c4"], "image_query": "dried dates", "image": {"provider": "commons", "asset_id": "152530325", "title": "File:Peeled and pitted dates.jpg", "description": "Peeled and pitted dates", "download_url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Peeled_and_pitted_dates.jpg/1920px-Peeled_and_pitted_dates.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "original_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/Peeled_and_pitted_dates.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "source_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peeled_and_pitted_dates.jpg", "credit": "Fumikas Sagisavas", "credit_line": "Own work", "license": "CC0", "license_url": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en", "attribution_required": "false", "restrictions": "", "date_created": "2024-09-12 09:47:12", "width": 1600, "height": 1600, "licensing_verified": false, "sha256": "eab02707541033f88ef707e23a9df96df6f416df9ab24d85b80bd4cf603d3012"}}], "sources": [{"id": "wiki-87598", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=87598", "text": "wild date palms.\nDate palms reach up to 30 metres (98 ft) in height, growing singly or in clumps with several stems\nfrom a single root system. Slow-growing, they can reach over 100 years of age when maintained properly. Their fruits are oval-cylindrical, 3\nto 7 centimetres (1 to 3 inches) long, and about 2.5 cm (1 in) in diameter, with colour ranging from dark brown\nto bright red or yellow, depending on variety. Containing 63\u201364% sugar by mass when dried, dates are consumed as sweet snacks on\ntheir own or with confections.\nThere is archaeological evidence of date cultivation in Arabia since the 6th millennium BCE. Dates are...\nnaturalised in many tropical and subtropical regions worldwide. P. dactylifera is the type species of genus Phoenix, which contains 12\u201319 species of\nwidely cultivated across northern Africa, the Middle East, Australia, South and Southeast Asia, the coastal Mediterranean basin, and Southern California. It is", "retrieved_text_sha256": "394b1d7009bfc97bfb0e46c073b1e7ace482beab5cc101a84c20ba991b90a95b"}], "research": {"event_date": null, "sensitive": false, "claims": [{"id": "c1", "fact": "\u0627\u0644\u0646\u062e\u0644\u0629 \u0645\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u064a\u0637\u0644\u0639 \u0637\u0648\u0644\u0647\u0627 \u0625\u0644\u0649 30 \u0645\u062a\u0631", "source_id": "wiki-87598", "quote": "wild date palms.\nDate palms reach up to 30 metres (98 ft) in height, growing singly or in clumps with several stems", "passage_id": "wiki-87598:p4"}, {"id": "c2", "fact": "\u0627\u0644\u0646\u062e\u0644\u0629 \u0628\u0637\u064a\u0626\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0645\u0648 \u0648\u0645\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u062a\u0639\u064a\u0634 \u0623\u0643\u062b\u0631 \u0645\u0646 100 \u0633\u0646\u0629 \u0625\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0647\u062a\u0645\u0648\u0627 \u0641\u064a\u0647\u0627 \u0628\u0634\u0643\u0644 \u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d", "source_id": "wiki-87598", "quote": "from a single root system. Slow-growing, they can reach over 100 years of age when maintained properly. Their fruits are oval-cylindrical, 3", "passage_id": "wiki-87598:p5"}, {"id": "c3", "fact": "\u062d\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0645\u0631 \u064a\u062a\u0631\u0627\u0648\u062d \u0637\u0648\u0644\u0647\u0627 \u0628\u064a\u0646 3 \u0625\u0644\u0649 7 \u0633\u0645 \u0648\u0642\u0637\u0631\u0647\u0627 \u062d\u0648\u0627\u0644\u064a 2.5 \u0633\u0645\u060c \u0648\u0623\u0644\u0648\u0627\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062a\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641 \u0645\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0646\u064a \u0627\u0644\u063a\u0627\u0645\u0642 \u0644\u0644\u0623\u062d\u0645\u0631 \u0623\u0648 \u0627\u0644\u0623\u0635\u0641\u0631 \u062d\u0633\u0628 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0648\u0639", "source_id": "wiki-87598", "quote": "to 7 centimetres (1 to 3 inches) long, and about 2.5 cm (1 in) in diameter, with colour ranging from dark brown", "passage_id": "wiki-87598:p6"}, {"id": "c4", "fact": "\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0645\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062c\u0641\u0641 \u064a\u062d\u062a\u0648\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0646\u0633\u0628\u0629 \u0633\u0643\u0631 \u0639\u0627\u0644\u064a\u0629 \u06